From: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: retain AN7563 basic Ethernet support

Adapt Ray Liu's AN7563 direct FE/QDMA implementation to the per-netdev
API. Enable the RX 2-byte offset to match the newer driver's NET_IP_ALIGN
buffer placement;
otherwise AN7563 DMA aligns the address down and drops the first two bytes
from frames delivered to the stack.
Pass DSA port tags through the TX descriptors. Hardware offload remains
unsupported on AN7563.

Link: https://github.com/iscle/openwrt/commit/44fb27a967
Signed-off-by: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_net.h>
 #include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
+#include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/regmap.h>
